{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the 31 October sprint report at head 3b8c2bd4, for request b3cf68d5 and review request 24934e1a. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, for four sentences. The rest of the report's facts that I checked match the record.\n\n## Changes I request\n\n1. The lead says: \"A person can now create a room on a deployed Worker, seed it, work in a provisioned fork...\" The script that does this is on no branch of main, and no person can run it from `main` today. The next sentence and the story are right. Say that a scratch room did this, and that the script is not landed.\n\n2. The S1 state is out of date. The story says \"The whole slice is in review\", and In progress says \"Whole S1 head: in review\". My verdict f23c7342 at 17:02 requested changes for the runbook and the note, before this head. Say: changes requested on the runbook and the note, with no change to the code. The commitment to review and land it can stay.\n\n3. The repair story says: \"A review of that head found that the diagnosis read an error's name twice.\" The record says otherwise. My approval 61a8c0ce missed it, and I corrected that approval in b1ba4dde after the builder found it. Say that the first approval missed it and the builder found it before landing. This is a checker miss, so it also belongs in \"What did not happen\".\n\n4. Decisions lists f71e8a29 as \"deployment waits for the witness\" with no qualifier. Ruling 90ee0518 replaced that item, and the deployment at 06:01 followed from that. Later rulings then held the Workers at 112eff12 until J4 closes. Say so, or drop the deployment clause, so that the list doesn't contradict the deployment table.\n\nOne further word, which I don't require but recommend: \"a room on this definition would lose its change cards\" comes from the builder's reading of the code, and nobody has run it. \"By reading the code\" keeps that label.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Landings: all sixteen heads, their times, their path counts and their commit counts, counted without the landing merge. The first lines of 147 and 588 code points are `871cdec9` and `112eff12`, and later subjects are within the limit.\n- Deployment: `112eff12`, the three Worker versions, and the hold on later deployments. No lockfile or migration path changes from 5dc9765f to `112eff12`. The only configuration path is the new `apps/room/wrangler.commons.jsonc`, which no deployed Worker in the table uses.\n- J4: setup closed in 44 s with 14 originals accepted, and in `public-setup-v15-1/result.json` the head and fork operations of both holds are confirmed on attempt 1. Five source reviews for setup: V7, V8, V9, V10 and V11.\n- S1: 42 phases and 5 minutes 29 seconds by receipts, the `agent-review` reason, the owner's review, the merge, the clone comparison, and the stop at `enrol-checker`.\n- Costs: S4's six and S6's seven review items match the lists in 2b29878c and 766b6c61. The failing test rate of 5 in 24 and the probe match the lost-abort note.\n- Decisions: 90ee0518, 2c938074, 4a276240, 2e2ccb6b, 8f2f7140 and 01b584e8 match, apart from item 4. So does dee246b9.\n- Misses: the gap in planner acts from 18:07 to 22:03 on 30 October fits the survey gap. The three wording repairs from 22:47 match c271830a.\n\nI did not confirm from the record the cause of the policy halt, the four-hour wait, the resident's 09:30 restart, or \"Publications from `destination@16` ... can now become confirmed\". That last sentence fits my BO1 review, but I traced no publication. I checked no prose in the Commons, causal-read or S2 stories beyond what my earlier reviews covered.\n\nA documents-only repair of these four sentences needs a diff review only.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: no code, no conclusion needed.\n- Security: no secret or private path in the report. Scope references are not in it.\n- Simplification: no objection. The level suits an adopter.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8bc8903782